.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH vissue 1  "vissue 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
vissue \- Plain\-text issue tracking over per\-project orgmode files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvissue\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plain\-text issue tracking over per\-project orgmode files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
Tracker root. Falls back to ISSUE_ROOT, VISSUE_ROOT, then the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Directory under the root holding one subdirectory per project. Falls back to VISSUE_PREFIX, then `prefix` in vissue.toml, then `Software`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
vissue\-create(1)
Create an issue. Pass the body with \-\-body or \-\-body\-file (`\-` reads stdin); omit both to leave the body empty for a later edit
.TP
vissue\-q(1)
Quick capture: create and print only the id
.TP
vissue\-list(1)
List issues, sorted by priority then state then id
.TP
vissue\-show(1)
Show one issue\*(Aqs metadata and file range
.TP
vissue\-update(1)
Update state, priority, or blocker edges
.TP
vissue\-ready(1)
Actionable issues: TODO or STARTED with no open blocker
.TP
vissue\-claim(1)
Take an issue: move it to STARTED and stamp the claim
.TP
vissue\-note(1)
Add a dated note to the top of an issue\*(Aqs logbook; state and claim untouched
.TP
vissue\-claims(1)
Every live claim, oldest first: who holds what, and for how long
.TP
vissue\-fold(1)
Fold an inbox org file: each unstamped `* TODO <title>` heading becomes an issue, then the heading is stamped with the id and flipped to DONE in place. Already\-stamped headings are skipped
.TP
vissue\-agenda(1)
Dated open work: deadlines and scheduled starts inside a horizon, overdue first
.TP
vissue\-hygiene(1)
Checklist for agents and CI: stalled claims plus corpus validation
.TP
vissue\-whoami(1)
Print the identity this tracker would record on a claim
.TP
vissue\-waiting\-on(1)
Issues waiting on this one
.TP
vissue\-body\-excerpt(1)
The first lines of an issue\*(Aqs file range
.TP
vissue\-search(1)
Substring search over ids, titles, properties, and bodies
.TP
vissue\-children(1)
Issues whose `:PARENT:` matches this id
.TP
vissue\-ancestors(1)
Blockers transitively required by this issue
.TP
vissue\-impact(1)
Issues transitively waiting on this issue
.TP
vissue\-related(1)
Explain bounded Org and lexical connections around an issue
.TP
vissue\-stale(1)
Open issues whose `:CREATED:` is older than N days
.TP
vissue\-count(1)
Print only the matching issue count
.TP
vissue\-export(1)
One JSON object per issue per line
.TP
vissue\-tree(1)
Children and blockers below an id
.TP
vissue\-cycles(1)
Cycles in the blocker graph
.TP
vissue\-graph(1)
The blocker and parent graph as Graphviz DOT
.TP
vissue\-refile(1)
Move an issue to another project\*(Aqs file
.TP
vissue\-backlinks(1)
Issues referring to this id
.TP
vissue\-roadmap(1)
A markdown roadmap of active and closed work
.TP
vissue\-check(1)
Validate the corpus. Exits non\-zero on any error
.TP
vissue\-digest(1)
A content digest of the corpus, for telling whether a copy is current
.TP
vissue\-mirror(1)
Write a read\-only projection of one or more projects to a file
.TP
vissue\-events(1)
Change events with a sequence above \-\-since
.TP
vissue\-ping(1)
Append a manual event, waking pollers without editing an issue
.TP
vissue\-wait(1)
Block until the generation passes \-\-last. Exits 2 on timeout
.TP
vissue\-gen(1)
Print the current generation counter
.TP
vissue\-projects(1)
List the projects found under the layout prefix
.TP
vissue\-identity(1)
Print the resolved binary, root, and prefix
.TP
vissue\-completions(1)
Write a shell completion script to stdout
.TP
vissue\-man(1)
Write the roff manual page to stdout
.TP
vissue\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
